# charset_e500.tab
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sharp pocket-computer (E500 family) character byte  <->  Unicode code point.
# Loaded at run time by ce140conv for text2bas / bas2text.
#
# Format (one mapping per line):
#     HH   U+XXXX      # Sharp byte HH maps to Unicode code point XXXX
#     HH   =           # explicitly undefined (keep the PUA round-trip fallback)
# '#' or ';' begins a comment. Blank lines are ignored.
#
# Any byte NOT listed here round-trips losslessly through the Private Use Area
# (byte 0xHH  <->  U+E000+HH), so bas2text -> text2bas stays byte-perfect even
# for glyphs still marked (verify) below.
#
# STATUS OF THIS TABLE
#   * 0x20-0x7E ASCII : CONFIRMED (handled in code, repeated here for clarity).
#   * 0xA1-0xDF katakana : the JIS X 0201 half-width layout. This is the common
#     convention for Sharp pocket computers but has NOT been byte-verified
#     against the E500 character-generator ROM. Marked (verify).
#   * 0x80-0xA0 / 0xE0-0xFF specials (Greek, math, box) : mostly left undefined.
#     Add rows here as you confirm them from the E500 ROM / manual.
# Correct any line and re-run; no recompile needed.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- ASCII (confirmed) -------------------------------------------------------
20 U+0020   # space
21 U+0021   # !
22 U+0022   # "
23 U+0023   # #
24 U+0024   # $
25 U+0025   # %
26 U+0026   # &
27 U+0027   # '
